mmdevapi, winecoreaudio: Implement IAudioEndpointVolume and apply volumes in software on macOS.
IAudioEndpointVolume was mostly stubs (GetChannelCount, channel levels, scalar levels,
steps, hardware support and notifications returned E_NOTIMPL), so programs that read
or set the device volume failed. Now:
- the channel count comes from the device's real mix format,
- master and per-channel levels (balance kept when the master moves), scalar <-> dB,
  mute, 2% volume steps and channel ranges work with Windows' return codes,
- the state is shared by all processes of the prefix (named section) and saved in
  HKCU\Software\Wine\MMDevAPI\EndpointVolume, like the persistent Windows volume,
- change notifications arrive on their own thread, also for changes from other
  processes, with the caller's event context,
- the endpoint volume is applied to every stream of the device (not to loopback).
winecoreaudio tried to set kAudioDevicePropertyVolumeScalar in the global scope, which
Mac output devices do not have, so session, stream and channel volumes (ISimpleAudioVolume,
IAudioStreamVolume, IChannelAudioVolume, mute) had no effect at all; where it did exist
it would have changed the Mac's own volume. The volumes are now applied to the samples
(8/16/24/32-bit PCM and float) for playback and recording; the Mac volume is untouched.
Test winrt/tests/audio.c: 73 checks, 0 failures (2-channel speakers, 1-channel microphone).

